TASK 29: RELATIONSHIP ANALYSIS

1. INTRODUCTION

Relationship Analysis is an important part of data analysis. It helps identify how two numerical variables are related. A scatter plot is used to represent the relationship between two variables visually.

2. OBJECTIVE

To create a scatter plot using Python and analyse the relationship between two numerical variables.

3. TOOLS AND TECHNOLOGIES

• Python
• Pandas
• Matplotlib
• Jupyter Notebook

4. DATASET DESCRIPTION

The Iris dataset was used for this task. A sample containing 10 observations was selected.

The following numerical columns were considered:

• Sepal Length
• Petal Length

5. IMPLEMENTATION

The dataset was loaded using the Pandas library. Two numerical columns were selected for analysis.

A scatter plot was created using Matplotlib's scatter() function. The correlation value was also calculated to understand the relationship between the selected variables.

6. OBSERVATIONS

1. The scatter plot visually represents the relationship between sepal length and petal length.
2. The selected variables generally increase together.
3. A positive relationship is observed between the two variables.

7. RESULT

A scatter plot was successfully created to visualize the relationship between sepal length and petal length.

The graph was saved as scatter_plot.png.

8. CONCLUSION

This task provided practical experience in visualizing relationships between numerical variables using Python. It helped develop an understanding of scatter plots, correlation, and data interpretation.

